{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["<b>And Isaac trembled with a great trembling, etc.</b> Isaac trembled two tremblings: one when he was bound [at the Akedah], and one here. And Scripture teaches you that this one was greater. And now, why did he tremble? Because he said in his heart: What sin and what stumbling-block was in my hand, that I blessed the younger before the elder? And Esau began to groan and said, etc., as Rashi explained, may his memory be for a blessing." "<b>Who then is he?</b> Isaac asked: Who will be firewood in Gehenna? And the holy spirit answered him: ״הוא הצד ציד״ — that is, Esau. And that is what Isaac said to Esau: ״ולכה איפה מה אעשה בני״ — that is, you are destined to be firewood in Gehenna; if so, what can I do for you?"], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:06:11.888912387Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}